findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading tests and implementation don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[MEDIUM] ServerError Display leaks raw server response\
    \ body \u2014 CWE-209 risk at error.rs:29' noting the body could contain internal\
    \ paths/stack traces. TEA also wrote CWE-209 tests for exit_codes.rs, but the\
    \ specific CliError Display leak to stderr was not directly flagged."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CRLF injection prevention tests for siem_client.rs (header\
    \ injection for X-Tenant-ID and Bearer token). Dev implemented the CRLF check.\
    \ However, the deeper issue of using raw String instead of validated TenantId\
    \ from axiathon-core was not caught \u2014 only the symptom (CRLF) was addressed,\
    \ not the root cause (type safety)."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. The reviewer noted the edition mismatch but not the dependency
    version drift issue.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[HIGH] RawConfig silently ignores unknown fields \u2014\
    \ no #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]' noting that typos like api_rul are silently\
    \ ignored. The token-in-config aspect was verified separately (token() returns\
    \ None unconditionally), but the silent ignore of the field was caught."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged '[MEDIUM] CRLF injection tests are vacuous \u2014 they\
    \ accept success' noting 'let _ = client; and pass... if someone removes the CRLF\
    \ check, the test still passes. These should assert!(result.is_err()).' Also flagged\
    \ env_axiathon_timeout_rejects_non_numeric as vacuous."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged the CRLF tests as having weak assertions: 'if construction\
    \ succeeds, they just let _ = client; and pass' \u2014 this is essentially a test\
    \ with no meaningful assertion on the success path, same pattern as I6."
